@@ -167,11 +190,55 @@ correctness headlessly/from a script rather than watching the window.
 
 ## Status
 
+**Roadmap phase 4: mesh -> Gaussian-splat resampling.** The deferred half of
+the splat work: `src/convert/mesh_to_gsplat.{h,cpp}` fits splats *to* a loaded
+GLB, where phase 3 could only import ones someone else had trained. Everything
+downstream of `GsplatAsset` was already agnostic about where splats came from,
+so this is a new producer plus wiring — `Representation::SplatFit` radio
+button, a splat-count slider, `--splat-fit=<count>`, and an "Export .ply"
+button backed by the new `src/io/gsplat_ply_writer.{h,cpp}` (with an
+`ITALY_SPLAT_EXPORT` hook so the export path is scriptable).
+
+Deliberately *not* the optimization-based fit the design doc deferred as
+research-grade. Area-weighted stratified sampling over the triangle soup
+(per-triangle quota from a rounded running area prefix, so counts are exact
+and deterministic; Hammersley points within each triangle, Cranley-Patterson
+rotated per triangle so regular meshes don't show a lattice), oriented to the
+interpolated shading normal, flattened along it, coloured by a bilinear
+base-colour texture sample at the splat's own UV. One global radius is
+correct because the sampling is area-uniform. 400k splats on `assets/test.glb`
+fit in well under a second — doctrine 2: a fit you can't re-run at every count
+isn't one you'd iterate on.
+
+Two renderer fixes were needed to make fitted splats render as anything, both
+of which also affect imported `.ply` scenes (more opaque, correctly so):
+
+- `__intersection__gsplat` reported the 3-sigma *shell* crossing, and
+  `__anyhit__gsplat` evaluates the Gaussian at whatever `t` it reports — so
+  every splat's alpha was pinned to `opacity * exp(-4.5)`, 1.1% of intended,
+  needing ~400 overlapping splats to look solid. Now reports the ray's
+  peak-density point (the standard 3DGS approximation, marked `realism:`).
+- That put the shading point deep inside the splat's own bounding ellipsoid,
+  which shadow rays treat as opaque (`traceOcclusion` disables any-hit), so a
+  fitted surface self-shadowed to black except at its silhouette. The
+  closest-hit gsplat branch now steps out along the normal by the ellipsoid's
+  own exact half-extent, the same class of fix the SDF branch already had.
+
+Verified visually (`ITALY_DUMP_FRAME` on `assets/test.glb --env=noon`) at 20k,
+200k, 400k and 1.2M splats: reads as the mesh's silhouette, albedo and shading
+with a soft splat texture, degrading gracefully to a soft blob at low counts
+rather than to holes. Round-tripped end to end — fit, `ITALY_SPLAT_EXPORT`,
+reload via `--gsplat=`, visually identical image. Host-side unit coverage in
+`tests/mesh_to_gsplat_test.cpp` (surface adherence, orientation, radius rule,
+determinism, degenerate input, writer/loader round-trip). Still not verified
+against a real captured/trained splat scene — no such asset lives in this repo
+yet, so the intersection fix's effect on one is reasoned, not observed.
+
 **Roadmap phase 3: Gaussian-splat import.** Imports pre-generated 3D
 Gaussian Splatting `.ply` scenes (the format `s-rank`'s triposplat and most
-3DGS trainers/exporters write) and renders them path-traced, not fit from a
-mesh — the design doc explicitly deferred mesh→3DGS fitting as its own
-research-grade problem. `src/io/gsplat_asset.h`/`gsplat_ply_loader.{h,cpp}`
+3DGS trainers/exporters write) and renders them path-traced. Fitting splats
+from a mesh was deferred at this point and landed later — see phase 4 above.
+`src/io/gsplat_asset.h`/`gsplat_ply_loader.{h,cpp}`
 parse the standard vertex layout (position, scale_0-2, rot_0-3, opacity,
 f_dc_0-2 — higher SH bands are read past but dropped, see the `realism:`
 note on `MATERIAL_GSPLAT`) and apply its activation functions once at
